    }
   ],
   "id": "rc:3256003872",
   "kind": "safety",
   "other_replies": [],
   "pin": null,
   "quote": "IIUC, this call could fail if a transaction is scanned where one of the P2TR outputs encodes an invalid x-only pubkey (i.e. not on the curve), so I suppose this should be changed to e.g. `if (!ret) co",
   "settled_by": {
    "at": "2026-05-18",
    "by": "Eunovo",
    "id": "rc:3260338373",
    "quote": "Changed to `if (!ret) continue;`"
   },
   "status": "resolved",
   "url": "https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/pull/35301#discussion_r3256003872"
  },
  {
   "after_reply": "likely_settled",
   "after_reply_note": "author fixed indexing",
   "association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
   "at": "2026-05-27",
   "author": "w0xlt",
   "author_replies": [
    "rc:3323906437"
   ],
   "blocking": false,
   "fix": {
    "at": null,
    "sha": "542475dce0fbaef13871cbb11b5b11992389633f"
   },
   "harm": "silent payment outputs mixed with regular outputs are assigned to contiguous indexes rather than preserving requested tx.vout positions",
   "hash": "8b7b9dcd2ba666c0",
   "history": [
    {
     "at": "2026-09-18T03:30:32+00:00",
     "blocking": false,
     "by": "run:20260918-0314",
     "cause": "rc:3314444642",
     "status": "resolved"
    }
   ],
   "id": "rc:3314444642",
   "kind": "correctness",
   "other_replies": [],
   "pin": null,
   "quote": "If SP outputs are mixed with regular outputs, callers would assign them to the wrong positions; the original map keys should be preserved.",
   "settled_by": {
    "at": "2026-05-29",
    "by": "Eunovo",
    "id": "rc:3323906437",
    "quote": "Done."
   },
   "status": "resolved",
   "url": "https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/pull/35301#discussion_r3314444642"
  },
  {
   "after_reply": "likely_settled",
   "after_reply_note": "author implemented skipping for unknown witness versions",
   "association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
   "at": "2026-05-28",
   "author": "w0xlt",
   "author_replies": [
    "rc:3323908625"
   ],
   "blocking": false,
   "fix": {
    "at": null,
    "sha": "542475dce0fbaef13871cbb11b5b11992389633f"
   },
   "harm": "transactions spending unknown SegWit version prevouts are not skipped as required by BIP352",
   "hash": "44528f5407a68fdb",
   "history": [
    {
     "at": "2026-09-18T03:30:32+00:00",
     "blocking": false,
     "by": "run:20260918-0314",
     "cause": "rc:3314571955",
     "status": "resolved"
    }
   ],
   "id": "rc:3314571955",
   "kind": "correctness",
   "other_replies": [],
   "pin": null,
   "quote": "BIP352 v0 says those transactions must be skipped entirely, so this should return no prevouts summary as soon as any spent prevout is witness v2+.",
   "settled_by": {
    "at": "2026-05-29",
    "by": "Eunovo",
    "id": "rc:3323908625",
    "quote": "Done."
   },
   "status": "resolved",
   "url": "https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/pull/35301#discussion_r3314571955"
  },
  {
   "after_reply": "likely_settled",
   "after_reply_note": "author enforced exact HRP and Bech32m",
   "association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
   "at": "2026-05-28",
   "author": "w0xlt",
   "author_replies": [
    "rc:3323907695"
   ],
   "blocking": false,
   "fix": {
    "at": null,
    "sha": "542475dce0fbaef13871cbb11b5b11992389633f"
   },
   "harm": "silent payment addresses without exact HRP or using standard Bech32 checksum instead of Bech32m would decode as valid",
   "hash": "1d18595a05c80c36",
   "history": [
    {
     "at": "2026-09-18T03:30:32+00:00",
     "blocking": false,
     "by": "run:20260918-0314",
     "cause": "rc:3314642210",
     "status": "resolved"
    }
   ],
   "id": "rc:3314642210",
   "kind": "correctness",
   "other_replies": [],
   "pin": null,
   "quote": "That can make spx... or Bech32-checksummed SP payloads decode as valid SP destinations, while BIP352 should require the exact SP HRP and Bech32m.",
   "settled_by": {
    "at": "2026-05-29",
    "by": "Eunovo",
    "id": "rc:3323907695",
    "quote": "Done."
   },
   "status": "resolved",
   "url": "https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/pull/35301#discussion_r3314642210"
  },
